@page "/ai/scenarios/custom-tool"
@inherits AppComponentBase

<PageOutlet Url="ai/scenarios/custom-tool"
            Title="Custom AI tool UI"
            Keywords="custom tool renderer, Blazor AI tool UI, BitAiRendererRegistry, RegisterTool, tool result card"
            Description="One AI tool rendered by an app's own Blazor component instead of the default card, everywhere that tool appears - bit BlazorUI's renderer registry." />

<DocsArticle Eyebrow="AI scenarios"
             Title="Custom tool UI"
             Lead="One tool rendered by an application component instead of the default card, everywhere that tool appears."
             GitHubUrl="AI/Scenarios/CustomTool/AiCustomToolScenarioPage.razor">

    <Badges>
        <BitTag Size="BitSize.Small" Variant="BitVariant.Outline" Color="BitColor.SecondaryForeground" Text="Bit.BlazorUI.AI" />
        <BitTag Size="BitSize.Small" Variant="BitVariant.Outline" Color="BitColor.SecondaryForeground" Text="Scripted transport" />
    </Badges>

    <ChildContent>
        <DocSection Id="demo" Title="Live demo"
                    Description="Search the documentation: search_docs reports its progress, then its hits, in a card of this site's own.">
            <DemoExample Title="A tool drawn by the app" RazorCode="@example1RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example1CsharpCode" CodeFiles="@example1CodeFiles" Id="example1">
                <AiScenarioFrame>
                    <BitAiChat Session="_session"
                               EmptyTitle="Search the documentation"
                               Suggestions="_suggestions" />
                </AiScenarioFrame>
            </DemoExample>
        </DocSection>

        <DocSection Id="how-it-works" Title="How it works">
            <p>
                <code>search_docs</code> is rendered by <code>SearchResultCard</code>, an ordinary component of this site.
                <code>BitAiRendererRegistry</code> maps a tool name to a renderer
                (<code>renderers.RegisterTool&lt;SearchResultCard&gt;("search_docs")</code>), so the substitution applies
                wherever that tool is called without touching the message list. The component is handed the call as its
                <code>Call</code> parameter and re-renders as the call changes: its progress reports while the tool runs, its
                result once it has returned. <code>RegisterTool(name, context =&gt; ...)</code> takes a render fragment
                instead, handed a <code>BitAiToolCallContext</code> (the call, its message and the session).
            </p>
            <p>
                The transport asks for <code>search_docs</code> as for any tool (see
                <BitLink Href="/ai/scenarios/tools">Tool calling</BitLink>), and the session runs it. The tool is declared
                with the <code>BitAiTool.Create&lt;TArgs&gt;(name, description, argumentsTypeInfo, (args, invocation, token) =&gt; ...)</code>
                overload (see <BitLink Href="/ai/scenarios/tools#declaring">Declaring a tool</BitLink>), whose handler is
                handed the <code>BitAiToolInvocation</code> and returns the whole outcome. It reports where it is through
                <code>invocation.Progress</code> - a <code>BitAiToolProgress</code> with a
                <code>Fraction</code> and a <code>Message</code>, which lands on the call as <code>Call.Progress</code> - and
                returns a full <code>BitAiToolOutcome</code>: the value the card reads (<code>Call.Result.Value</code>), the
                <code>Text</code> the model reads, and the <code>Citations</code> of what it searched, which the session adds
                to the reply's sources. The card reads the arguments through <code>Call.DisplayArguments</code>, which holds
                them while they still stream, and the time the call took through <code>Call.Duration</code>.
            </p>
            <p>
                A custom renderer is handed data a model produced, so the shape it wants is a hope, not a guarantee: the card
                checks the payload before it reads it, and a renderer that throws anyway is contained by the boundary around
                it rather than taking the conversation down. The same registry takes renderers for message part kinds,
                artifact kinds, structured output schemas, code languages and citations.
            </p>
        </DocSection>

        <DocSection Id="components" Title="Components used">
            <ul>
                <li><BitLink Href="/components/ai/toolcallview"><code>BitAiToolCallView</code></BitLink> - the view that hands the call to the registered renderer.</li>
                <li><BitLink Href="/components/ai/rendererboundary"><code>BitAiRendererBoundary</code></BitLink> - what keeps a failing renderer to itself.</li>
                <li><BitLink Href="/components/ai/messagepartview"><code>BitAiMessagePartView</code></BitLink> - the dispatcher every part goes through.</li>
                <li><BitLink Href="/components/ai/sourcelist"><code>BitAiSourceList</code></BitLink> - the source the tool's result cites, under the reply.</li>
            </ul>
        </DocSection>
    </ChildContent>

    <FooterTemplate>
        <DocPager Pages="AiScenarioNav.Items" AriaLabel="AI scenarios" />
    </FooterTemplate>
</DocsArticle>
